{"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"One particularly damaging, but often ignored, effect of conflict on education is the proliferation of attacks on schools[…]as children, teachers or school buildings become the targets of attacks. Parents fear sending their children to school. Girls are particularly vulnerable to sexual violence.","ref":"2013 July 19, Mark Tran, “Denied an education by war”, in The Guardian Weekly, volume 189, number 6, page 1:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[136,144]]}],"glosses":["A person who teaches, especially one employed in a school; preceptor."]},{"glosses":["The index finger; the forefinger."]},{"examples":[{"text":"But if the last two years are a teacher, look for the bombastic tweets to resume before sunrise.","ref":"2017 February 28, Steve LeVine, “Trump Speech to Congress: The Message Was Trumpian, But The Tone Was Decidedly Not”, in Quartz:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[32,39]]}],"glosses":["An indication; a lesson."]},{"raw_glosses":["(Mormonism) The second highest office in the Aaronic priesthood, held by priesthood holders of at least the age of 14."],"glosses":["The second highest office in the Aaronic priesthood, held by priesthood holders of at least the age of 14."],"tags":["Mormonism"]}],"pos":"noun","head_templates":[{"name":"en-noun","args":{},"expansion":"teacher (plural teachers)"}],"forms":[{"form":"teachers","tags":["plural"]}],"translations":[{"lang":"French","code":"fr","lang_code":"fr","sense":"person who teaches","tags":["masculine"],"word":"professeur"},{"lang":"French","code":"fr","lang_code":"fr","sense":"person who teaches","tags":["masculine"],"word":"maître d'école"},{"lang":"French","code":"fr","lang_code":"fr","sense":"person who teaches","tags":["masculine"],"word":"enseignant"},{"lang":"French","code":"fr","lang_code":"fr","sense":"person who teaches","english":"primary school","translation":"primary school","word":"instituteur"},{"lang":"German","code":"de","lang_code":"de","sense":"pers